(a) whether any assessment has been carried out regarding the impact of Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samruddhi Kendras (PMKSKs) on the distribution of agricultural inputs and delivery of farmer services in the State of Madhya Pradesh;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the extent to which PMKSKs have facilitated access to soil testing, advisory services and awareness about various Government schemes;
(d) whether PMKSKs have contributed to strengthening the operational viability of the Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) in the State of Madhya Pradesh; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the adequacy of food processing and value addition infrastructure in the major agricultural producing regions of Punjab, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any gaps have been identified in the cold-chain infrastructure, agro-processing facilities and post-harvest value addition capacity across the State, if so, the details thereof along with the corrective measures taken in this regard; and
(c) whether any proposals for the creation or expansion of food processing infrastructure in Punjab are under consideration, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the Central assistance sanctioned, released and utilised during the last four years under the crop diversification and crop residue management programmes in Punjab, along with the objectives, implementing agencies and physical progress thereunder, district-wise;
(b) the targets fixed, achievements made, shortcomings and the reasons therefor in Punjab, district-wise; and
(c) the details of the corrective measures taken/proposed to be taken in consultation with Government of Punjab to address these shortcomings and the current status of their implementation?

(a) the manner in which Government plans to expand the newly introduced 'Viksit Bharat Youth Parliament' scheme format to non-collegiate rural institutions during the current Financial Year;
(b) the number of female students wining top honors during the national-level evaluation round;
(c) whether the integrated online evaluation portal has successfully automated institutional registrations screening process to prevent region-wise participation backlogs;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) the details of the allocation made and released to State coordinators for organizing localized mock parliament sessions in aspirational districts; and
(f) the enhancements introduced to translate official resource training-materials into all 22 scheduled regional-languages this quarter, if any?

(a) the number of cases taken up and disposed of through e-Lok Adalats during the last three years, State-wise and year wise;
(b) the total amount of monetary settlement arrived through e-Lok Adalats during the said period;
(c) the States/Union Territories where e-Lok Adalats have been introduced or expanded during the said period; and
(d) the further steps proposed to expand this initiative across the country?

(a) the mission-wise status of deployment of Global Passport Seva Programme (GPSP V2.0) across Indian Embassies and Consulates;
(b) the number of overseas Indian nationals served through this programme, so far, country-wise;
(c) the specific technical or administrative challenges faced in extending this service to all diplomatic missions; and 
(d) the countries identified for extension of the programme in the near future and the timeline proposed for the same?

(a) the specific welfare and development schemes implemented for the Sikh minority community during 2025–26;
(b) the steps taken for the preservation and development of the religious and cultural heritage sites of the Sikh community, including gurdwaras and affiliated institutions;
(c) the progress made in the implementation of the Prime Minister's New 15-Point Programme for Sikh community; and
(d) whether Government is proposing to launch any new initiatives or enhancements for the Sikh minority in the coming years, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the implementation framework of the revised BharatNet project has been implemented across the country and if so, the details of State-wise progress achieved under it up to June 2026;
(b) the details of optical fibre infrastructure developed under the BharatNet project, including the number of connected Gram Panchayats and the expansion of optical fibre network, so far; and
(c) the measures taken for rapid expansion of indigenous 4G and 5G networks, including the progress achieved therein?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken initiatives to strengthen welfare, protection and consular assistance for Indians residing, working or travelling abroad and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the role of e-Migrate ecosystem in ensuring safe, transparent and orderly overseas employment for emigrant workers;
(c) whether new institutional or technological mechanisms have improved coordination among Indian Missions and Posts during distress situations and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to enhance outreach and effectiveness of welfare, consular and community support programmes for overseas Indians?

(a) the sanctioned strength, actual strength and vacancies in various Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) as on date;
(b) the Force-wise details thereof, including the Central Reserve Police Force, Border Security Force, Central Industrial Security Force, Indo-Tibetan Border Police and Sashastra Seema Bal; 
(c) the number of recruitments made during each of the last five years and the current year and State-wise breakup of such recruitments; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to fill vacancies and improve operational capacity of the Forces?

(a) the progress made under the World's Largest Grain Storage Plan (WLGSP) in the cooperative sector during the last one year;
(b) the number of PACS selected for creation of storage infrastructure under the programme, State-wise;
(c) the details of storage capacity created and expenditure incurred under the scheme so far; and
(d) the expected impact of the programme on reducing post-harvest losses and strengthening food security in the country?

(a) the  cumulative account enrolment under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) and Jan Suraksha Schemes, State-wise and gender-wise;
(b) the total quantum of loans disbursed under the MUDRA scheme, along with category-wise details for SC/ST/OBC and women borrowers and the status of sanctions under the ‘Tarun Plus’ category; and
(c) the current NPA position under the scheme and the trend during the last three financial years?

(a) the total volume and value of real-time transactions processed through the Unified Payments Interface (UPI) compared to global payment gateways;
(b) the fiscal incentives provided over the last five years to accelerate digital payment infrastructure in rural areas; and
(c) whether international agreements have operationalised UPI transactions across foreign jurisdictions?

(a) the total allocation of foodgrains and central assistance provided to the States under the Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PMGKAY) during the last three financial years, State-wise;
(b) the number of ineligible beneficiaries identified and removed from the ration card database in the States under the Rightful Targeting exercise, State-wise;
(c) whether the NIRMAL real-time verification architecture has been integrated with databases available in the States for continuous beneficiary verification, State-wise; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the impact on improving transparency in the Public Distribution System?

(a) the year-wise reduction in imports of key technical-grade pesticides, dyes and chemical intermediates since 2014, along with the major reasons therefor;
(b) the current status of the proposed Production-Linked Incentive (PLI) framework aimed at promoting domestic feedstock manufacturing, including the progress made so far and the likely timeline for its implementation; and
(c) whether Government has undertaken digital safety compliance audits in units handling hazardous chemicals with a view to reducing industrial accidents, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of implementation of the Sub-Mission on Agricultural Mechanization (SMAM) in Punjab during the last three years;
(b) whether any review has been conducted regarding the progress of various components of the scheme in Punjab, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the extent of adoption of Custom Hiring Centres, Farm Machinery Banks, Kisan Drone Services and other mechanization initiatives supported under the scheme in Punjab; and
(d) whether any priority areas have been identified under the revised SMAM guidelines to strengthen agricultural mechanization in Punjab, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the extent to which the beneficiaries of Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises Scheme (PMFME) in Punjab have availed the credit-linked subsidies, seed capital assistance, training, branding, and marketing support under the scheme;
(b) whether common infrastructure facilities, incubation centers, and ODOP-based processing units envisaged under the scheme have been established in all districts of Punjab, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether any recommendations have been received to improve implementation and increase the participation of micro-enterprises, self-help groups, farmer producer organizations, and cooperatives under the scheme in Punjab, if so, the details of measures taken in this regard?

(a) the  details regarding the number of beneficiaries covered under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) scheme in Punjab and the amount disbursed under the scheme during the last four years, year-wise;
(b) whether any assessment has been conducted regarding the utilization of PM-KISAN assistance by farmers in Punjab for agricultural inputs and allied agricultural activities, if so, the details thereof; and 
(c) whether any measures have been taken to ensure the seamless transfer of benefits to eligible farmers and to improve the identification of beneficiaries in Punjab, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note of delays in implementation or non-completion of projects sanctioned in Punjab under the Khelo India Scheme and other Central sports schemes during the last four years; 
(b) if so, the year-wise details of the amount sanctioned, released and spent; 
(c) the number of projects completed, under progress and pending; and 
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure timely implementation of the projects?

(a) whether Government has observed the use of darknet, encrypted communication applications and cryptocurrency-based transactions in drug trafficking cases detected in Punjab;
(b) if so, the measures being taken to identify and disrupt such trafficking networks;
(c) whether any trend of the use of digital platforms in cross-border drug trafficking and distribution networks has come to light; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken to strengthen cyber, forensic and technical capabilities for investigation?

(a) the city-wise details of the number of projects sanctioned, sanctioned cost, funds released, expenditure incurred, and physical progress achieved during the last three years under the Smart City Mission (SCM) in Amritsar, Jalandhar, and Ludhiana;
(b) the number of projects completed, under construction, and pending so far, city-wise;
(c) the details of the names of pending projects, sanctioned costs, expenditure incurred to date, and current physical progress; and
(d) the details of the proposed timelines for the completion of pending projects, project-wise?

(a) the details of assessment made, identified gaps, district-wise findings and proposed corrective measures taken by the Central Government regarding groundwater conservation, crop diversification and regulation of groundwater exploitation in the State of Punjab;
(b) the details of the advisories, recommendations and directives issued to the Punjab Government in this regard, the action taken by State Government regarding the same and the current status of compliance thereof; and
(c) the district-wise details of the State's over-exploited groundwater blocks, the actions taken for groundwater restoration and the proposed measures to ensure adherence to timelines and accountability?
